      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Toronto Maple Leafs didn't just shuffle the roster this offseason - they detonated the old foundation and rebuilt with foot speed, bold bets, and a two-time Stanley Cup champion in the crease. <strong>Sergei Bobrovsky has agreed to a three-year, $21M deal with the Maple Leafs</strong>, a signing GM John Chayka called \"a lot done\" after a wild free agency and trade day. The Leafs, who finished 8th in the Atlantic with 78 points and a brutal L7 streak to end their season, are now an improved team year over year - most notably in their foot speed after adding Gavin McKenna first overall in the 2026 Draft, Nick Paul via trade, and Brandon Duhaime on a three-year deal. Bobrovsky, 37, brings Cup-winning pedigree but also age risk; the question isn't whether the Leafs took a chance - it's whether they can extract elite value before the wheels fall off. <strong>What to watch: how the Bobrovsky signing reshapes the crease hierarchy and whether the Leafs' new core of youth and speed can finally break their playoff drought</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated July 2, 2026"
      },
