      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "Packed houses and high expectations met a stress-free day of baseball at Rogers Centre, finally giving Toronto a reason to breathe. <strong>Sean Keys launched his first career Major League home run on Canada Day</strong>, a three-run shot that flipped the game from 2-0 to 5-0 and broke the Mets wide open in a 9-3 rout. This victory snaps a two-game slump against New York and lifts the Blue Jays to a 41-46 record, keeping them third in the AL East but still 11 games behind the division leader. Rookie Keys, who flashed 98 mph velocity on the mound alongside Spencer Miles' three scoreless innings, is the story right now - showing the kind of progress Guerrero Jr. has been missing. The team sits on a one-game win streak, proving they can still dig out of this hole for a Wild Card run. <strong>Saturday's 9:10 PM ET trip to Seattle at 7/4 marks the next critical test</strong> as the Jays look to build momentum before the All-Star break.",
        "updated": "Updated July 2, 2026"
