      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "The Toronto Raptors' offseason has exploded into a storyline of legendary returns and shocking departures, with the franchise's future hanging on a single, seismic gamble. <strong>Kawhi Leonard reportedly wants to retire as a Raptor</strong>, a declaration that could reshape the entire Atlantic Division if he indeed returns to the team that once crowned him champion. The Raptors, who finished 46-36 and third in the Atlantic Division before their season ended, now face a cap and roster picture that could swing wildly depending on whether Leonard's wish becomes reality. Gradey Dick's farewell adds another layer of transition, while Alijah Martin's two-year lock-in signals a commitment to young depth. The front office isn't just tinkering; it's betting on legacy, on emotion, and on a player who once defined Toronto's basketball identity. <strong>What happens next with Kawhi Leonard's retirement wish will determine whether the Raptors rebuild around history or pivot toward a new era</strong>. The coming days of free agency won't just fill roster spots - they'll decide the soul of the franchise.",
        "updated": "Updated July 2, 2026"
      },
